    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0b56835b-4565-5c7b-80c0-7d2c96cafb05",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2004$, there were approximately $8560$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $0.5\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2016$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=8560$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-0.5/100=-0.005$. The elapsed time is $t=2016-2004=12$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 8560e^{(-0.005)(12)} \\\\\n&= 8560e^{-0.06} \\\\\n&= 8560(0.9417645\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 8062\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $8062$ crimes occurred in $2016$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
