    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dfba2c82-a6bd-59de-a736-1e56ef425c23",
      ":question/problem": "In medieval times, there were $4680$ people living in a city struck by a plague. If the disease resulted in a daily *decrease* in the population at a continuously compounded rate of $1.6\\%$, what was the city's population after $3$ weeks? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=4680$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-1.6/100=-0.016$. The rate is daily, so convert the duration to days: $t=3\\times 7=21$ days.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 4680e^{(-0.016)(21)} \\\\\n&= 4680e^{-0.336} \\\\\n&= 4680(0.7146231\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 3344\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ weeks, the population was approximately $3344$ people.",
