    "question": {
      ":question/id": "92114d69-6764-56df-a9b0-7bb5eee6bd1f",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2008$, there were approximately $2390$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $4.6\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2014$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=2390$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-4.6/100=-0.046$. The elapsed time is $t=2014-2008=6$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 2390e^{(-0.046)(6)} \\\\\n&= 2390e^{-0.276} \\\\\n&= 2390(0.7588129\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 1814\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $1814$ crimes occurred in $2014$.",
